From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FerrionOS contributors <contributors@ferrion.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:05:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] backend: Run ferrion-wm on FerrionOS with timed CPU
 presentation

Gate tty, winit and system Wayland independently, including libinput in
the config crate. Add the native inputd/DRM adapter using one Smithay,
surfaceless EGL, the cursor plane and measured redraw deadlines. Send
frame callbacks and feedback after handoff. Keep the layout code intact.

Default Linux features preserve the original integrations. Target cooks
and four fixture layouts run; the ten-boot acceptance series follows.
Use the ferrion-wm name for the executable and visible interface.
